    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <h3>What types of roof ventilation are recommended in Tampa Bay?</h3>
        <p>In Tampa Bay, ridge vents, soffit vents, and solar attic fans are commonly recommended roof ventilation systems. These options provide effective airflow in our warm and humid climate and work well with various roof types, including those covered with products from Owens Corning, GAF, and Gulf Coast Supply, and especially those with tile like the ones from Verea.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>How does roof ventilation impact energy efficiency?</h3>
        <p>Proper roof ventilation significantly impacts energy efficiency by reducing cooling costs. It allows hot air to escape and cooler air to circulate, which can lessen the load on air conditioning systems, keeping your home comfortable and your energy bills from skyrocketing.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Can improper roof ventilation lead to mold issues?</h3>
        <p>Yes, poor roof ventilation can create an environment conducive to mold growth by trapping moisture in your attic space. This can lead to mold issues that not only affect the structural integrity of your home but also the health of its occupants.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
